\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs36 iFinance Books\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 A beginner guide: register, log in, and work inside the application\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Written for new team members. Explains what the product is, what you can do after signing in, and what the software does behind the scenes.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 1. What this project is\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Think of iFinance Books as the office computer system of a vehicle finance shop. People take a two-wheeler on hire-purchase (HP) and pay a monthly EMI. Staff collect money, keep other books, and produce reports.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Technically it is a website (React) talking to a server (Express) that stores data in PostgreSQL.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 2. Register and log in\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 On the login page you see Sign in and Register.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Register: name, username, password, role. Password is hashed. You get a token stored in the browser for 7 days.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Log in: username and password. Same token if the password matches.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Demo accounts: admin, clerk, line \u8212? password demo123.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Roles are named but the app looks almost the same for everyone. Register can even create ADMIN. After login you land on the Dashboard.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 3. The screen you live in\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Navbar: Transactions, Others, Finance's, search, Settings, Log out.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Search looks across customers, bikes, accounts, journals, and modules.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 4. Dashboard\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Tiles: Income, Expenses, EMI Collection, HP HL Collection (mostly outstanding handloans), OD Collection, Closed HPs. Click a tile or folder to open that area.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 5. Finances (the main job)\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Finance list: search HP accounts. New Finance creates a customer, EMI timetable, and an RTA row.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Customer tabs:\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Overview \u8212? edit customer; seize or close.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Receipt \u8212? collect EMI; numbered receipt; pays oldest unpaid EMI first; printable slip.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Bills \u8212? receipt history and reprint.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  EMI Reports / OD's \u8212? schedule and overdue interest (default 0.1 percent per day).\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Out Payment / Hand Loans \u8212? extra money out or informal loan.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  STM \u8212? settlement and close. RMD \u8212? reminders. Seized/Closed \u8212? status view.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 6. Other books and lists\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Transactions: HandLoans, Consultancy (used bikes), Capitals, Deposits, Cheques, Bank, Chits, Loans, Credits, Investments, Assets, Inc & Exp, Journals.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Others: Income & Expense bills, RTA, All Accounts, Sub Masters, Trial Balance, Agents, Branches. Agents/RTA/Branches are simple lists, not live government systems.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 7. Reports and accounting\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Working reports: Day Report, Line Report, Collection, OD, Closed HP, Seized HP, P&L, Balance Sheet, Trial Balance, Charts. Grey names in the catalogue are not built yet.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Accounting: every rupee is debit and credit. Journals can be automatic (receipts) or manual, and can be reversed.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 8. Admin\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Users (ADMIN can create), Settings (OD percent, settlement, day-scroll protect, company address), Support (read-only company details).\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 9. What happens inside (four engines)\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  EMI engine: monthly due dates when you create a finance.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Collection engine: receipt reduces unpaid EMIs, updates bank, posts journal, refreshes dashboard.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Overdue engine: interest is calculated when you open OD screens, not stored as its own table.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Refresh engine: dashboard tiles and charts are recalculated after many saves.\par
\pard\sa120\fs22 Flow: Browser -> API with token -> Express on port 4000 -> PostgreSQL.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 10. A day in the office\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Log in. New Finance. Collect Receipt. Check OD. Seize or STM if needed. Enter expenses. Day Report. Line Report for tomorrow. Journals / P&L for accounts.\par
\pard\sb280\sa120\b\fs22 11. Not fully built\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\sa60\fs22 \bullet  Many report names are grey. No SMS/email/KYC upload. Roles barely restrict screens. Receipts cannot be voided from the UI.\par
